protester|public-objector|NOUN|person publicly objecting to something|A person who publicly shows opposition to an action, policy, or situation.|người biểu tình; người phản đối công khai|A protester held a sign asking for cleaner water.|Một người biểu tình cầm biển yêu cầu nước sạch hơn.|Countable; protester against a policy identifies the object of opposition, but not every protester belongs to one organization.|0
skeletal|bones-related|ADJECTIVE|relating to the body's skeleton|Relating to the bones that form the supporting framework of a body.|thuộc bộ xương; liên quan đến xương|The diagram labels the main skeletal structures.|Sơ đồ ghi tên các cấu trúc chính của bộ xương.|Usually before a noun such as structure or system; this sense concerns anatomy rather than an extremely thin appearance.|-
willpower|self-control|NOUN|determination to control actions|The determination to control your actions and keep working towards a chosen goal.|ý chí; sức mạnh tự chủ|It took willpower to keep practising when progress was slow.|Cần có ý chí để tiếp tục luyện tập khi tiến bộ chậm.|Uncountable; willpower can support persistence but does not guarantee success or remove every obstacle.|-
drum|musical-instrument|NOUN|instrument played by striking a stretched surface|A musical instrument played by striking a stretched surface, usually over a hollow body.|trống|The drummer tapped the drum softly before the song began.|Người chơi trống gõ nhẹ lên trống trước khi bài hát bắt đầu.|Countable; play the drums commonly refers to a set of percussion instruments.|0
fierce|intense|ADJECTIVE|very strong or intense|Very strong or intense, especially in force or competition.|dữ dội; quyết liệt|A fierce wind pushed against the windows all night.|Một cơn gió dữ dội thổi vào các cửa sổ suốt đêm.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; fierce competition concerns intensity rather than an animal's aggression.|0
fierce|aggressive|ADJECTIVE|ready to attack or show anger|Showing strong aggression or appearing ready to attack.|hung dữ; dữ tợn|The fierce dog growled when strangers approached the gate.|Con chó hung dữ gầm gừ khi người lạ đến gần cổng.|Can describe an animal, person, or expression; appearance alone need not establish that an attack occurs.|1
